# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ovoz AI — environment
# Every value below is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the platform
# runs end-to-end on its built-in local engines (see README ▸ Engines).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Signing key for session cookies. Auto-generated into data/.secret if unset.
OVOZ_SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Language model ───────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, answer generation switches from the local extractive
# synthesiser to Claude. Everything else keeps working either way.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Default claude-opus-5. Voice traffic that needs the lowest possible
# time-to-first-word can set claude-haiku-4-5 here instead.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ── Gemini (Google) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Alternative LLM. When GEMINI_API_KEY is set, answer generation uses Gemini
# (called over the REST API — no extra dependency). Falls back to the local
# engine on any error, exactly like the Claude path.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# A flash model is recommended for voice latency; thinking is turned off
# automatically for flash models to minimise time-to-first-word.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# Force one engine regardless of which keys are present:
#   local | anthropic | gemini   (unset ⇒ first key found, Gemini before Claude)
LLM_PROVIDER=

# ── Embeddings ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, the hybrid retriever swaps its local hashed-ngram encoder
# for hosted embeddings. Dimensions are detected automatically.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small

# ── Telephony (Twilio Elastic SIP Trunking) ──────────────────
# Unset ⇒ the built-in call simulator drives the voice pipeline.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=

# ── Speech (internal Uzbek STT/TTS) ──────────────────────────
# Browser Web Speech API is used for Russian/English in the Playground with no
# key. For Uzbek, set these to route to the internal models. Unset ⇒ Uzbek also
# uses the browser voice.
#
# STT (speech → text): no auth, accepts a multipart WAV `file`, returns {text}.
# This is the Uzbek model (Kotib) — it knows only Uzbek.
STT_TRANSCRIBE_URL=
# Optional second engine: any OpenAI-compatible /audio/transcriptions endpoint
# (Whisper turbo). Covers Russian, English and everything else. When BOTH are
# set and the agent is Uzbek-primary, the two run CONCURRENTLY on the same
# utterance and the better transcript wins — which is how a caller who switches
# language mid-sentence gets understood. Running both costs max(a,b), not a+b.
WHISPER_TRANSCRIBE_URL=
WHISPER_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo
# Only needed if the Whisper endpoint requires a bearer token.
WHISPER_API_KEY=
# TTS (text → speech): JWT-protected. Provide TTS_CLIENT_SECRET and the server
# mints & auto-refreshes its own 24h token; or paste a ready TTS_JWT_TOKEN.
TTS_BASE_URL=
TTS_CLIENT_ID=frontend
TTS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TTS_JWT_TOKEN=                 # alternative to the secret (expires in ~24h)
# Real profiles on the server; the agent's voice maps here by gender
# (Nilufar → female, Timur → male).
TTS_VOICE_FEMALE=uz_female_calm
TTS_VOICE_MALE=uz_male_news

# ── Telephony bridge (Asterisk / FreePBX via AudioSocket) ────
# Puts live SIP calls on the internal Uzbek STT/TTS + runTurn engine instead of
# Twilio's built-in speech. The standalone bridge (see telephony-bridge/README.md)
# streams AudioSocket audio to /api/telephony/bridge/{turn,end}, authenticated by
# this shared secret. Unset ⇒ those endpoints return 503 (bridge disabled).
BRIDGE_SHARED_SECRET=
# The bridge PROCESS has its own env (AUDIOSOCKET_PORT, NEXT_BASE_URL, VAD_*,
# FILLER_AFTER_MS, BRIDGE_TO_NUMBER, …) documented in telephony-bridge/README.md
# — not loaded here.
#
# Fixed lines (greetings, re-prompts, the "bir daqiqa" holding lines) are
# rendered once and cached as raw PCM under data/tts-cache/. Deleting that
# directory is always safe; it refills on demand.

# ── Developer API (/v1) & webhooks ───────────────────────────
# The /v1/* REST API authenticates with per-tenant API keys (ovoz_sk_…) created in
# the console Developers panel; webhooks POST signed payloads (x-ovoz-signature:
# sha256=HMAC) to URLs registered there. Both are always on — nothing to set here.
# See INTEGRATION.md for the partner-developer guide.






# sudo systemctl restart ovoz
# sudo systemctl status ovoz
# journalctl -u ovoz -f

# ~/deploy.sh

# cd ~/president-ai-award && npm run build && sudo systemctl restart ovoz      rebuiilds